meta {
  name: A forged token is refused
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiIxMTExMTExMS0xMTExLTExMTEtMTExMS0xMTExMTExMTExMTEifQ.not-a-real-signature
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 401
}

docs {
  The signature is checked against the project's JWKS, and the algorithm comes from the
  **key**, never from the token's own header. Trusting the header is the classic
  algorithm-confusion attack: flip `alg` to HS256 and sign with the public key as the
  shared secret. Pinning to the key's algorithm makes that impossible to express.
}
